    <string-array name="tut_first_drawing_steps">
        <item>On the home screen, tap New Drawing, pick a canvas size and tap Create.</item>
        <item>Choose the Brush, Pencil or Pen tool from the toolbar. Tap the selected tool again to open its brush library.</item>
        <item>Tap the color circle at the bottom to pick a color from the wheel, sliders, HEX code or a palette.</item>
        <item>Use the side sliders to change brush size and opacity. Pinch with two fingers to zoom and rotate the canvas.</item>
        <item>Made a mistake? Tap Undo, or tap the canvas with two fingers. GoDraw saves automatically.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tut_layers_steps">
        <item>Open Layers from the bottom bar. The top layer in the list is drawn in front.</item>
        <item>Tap + to add a layer. Draw line art on one layer and color on a layer below it.</item>
        <item>Use the eye icon to hide a layer and the lock to protect it from changes.</item>
        <item>Long-press the handle on the left of a layer and drag it to change the order.</item>
        <item>Adjust opacity and blend mode for the selected layer, or merge it down when you are done.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tut_animation_steps">
        <item>Create a New Animation. The timeline appears above the bottom bar.</item>
        <item>Draw the first pose, then tap Add frame and draw the next pose.</item>
        <item>Turn on onion skin to see the previous frame in red and the next frame in blue.</item>
        <item>Press Play to watch your animation. Change the frame rate with the FPS button.</item>
        <item>Use Duplicate frame to start a new drawing from the current one, and drag frames to reorder them.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tut_keyframes_steps">
        <item>Draw an object on its own layer, then open Animate from the bottom bar.</item>
        <item>Go to the first frame and tap Key all to remember the layer\'s starting position.</item>
        <item>Move to a later frame, choose Animate on canvas and drag the layer to a new position.</item>
        <item>GoDraw fills in every frame in between. Choose an easing to make the motion feel natural.</item>
        <item>Try a transition such as Fade in to add keyframes in one tap.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tut_gestures_steps">
        <item>Two-finger pinch zooms and rotates the canvas; two-finger drag moves it.</item>
        <item>Tap with two fingers to undo and with three fingers to redo.</item>
        <item>Long-press the canvas with your finger to pick a color.</item>
        <item>With a stylus, pressure changes brush size and opacity. The stylus button can switch to the eraser.</item>
        <item>Turn on palm rejection in Settings so your hand does not leave marks while you draw.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tut_export_steps">
        <item>Tap the export icon at the top of the editor.</item>
        <item>Choose PNG, transparent PNG or JPG for pictures, and GIF or MP4 for animations.</item>
        <item>Pick a resolution and frame rate. MP4 exports include your imported audio.</item>
        <item>Export to your Gallery or choose a location, then share the result directly.</item>
        <item>Exports from every plan, including Free, never have a watermark.</item>
    </string-array>
</resources>
